WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.340
Hello and welcome to my talk.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.430
Dissecting the
quick fix, analyzing

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:12.680
tech-solutionist solutions.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.100
Let me start with a definition.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.120
What is tech solutionism?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.540
Tech solutionism is the
tendency to use technology

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.380
to solve a societal, political,
organizational, environmental, ...

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.630
... what have you problem.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.660
A few examples should
make this more clear.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:33.140
Example number one: riots.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.440
What's the problem?

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:37.900
Well... suppressed population
groups, for example,

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:41.380
ethnic minorities are
starting to mobilize.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.670
What do we observe?

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.980
This is more likely to
happen when it's hot.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.680
Very hot.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.930
What is the solution?

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:53.020
Well - just install
acclimatization throughout!

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.150
And what do we gain?

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.740
We don't have to
actually address

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.960
those groups' demands.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.080
Example two: mass shootings.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.590
What is the problem?

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:05.050
Since 2014, on
average, there has

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:08.570
been more than one mass
shooting a day in the US.

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:10.490
What do we observe?

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:14.110
You can't always see if
someone's carrying a gun.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:16.000
What's the solution?

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.030
Well - just install advanced
surveillance technology.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:20.420
And what do we gain?

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:24.780
We don't have to change the
laws related to gun ownership.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:28.500
Example number three:
climate change.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.480
What is the problem?

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:33.480
Climate change is rendering
parts of the Earth inhabitable

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:36.880
and strongly impacts living
conditions in others.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:39.040
What's our observation?

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.470
Time is passing and we
are less and less on track

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:44.750
to keep the situation
under control.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.640
What's the solution?

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.080
Well, we just move to Mars
or somewhere else in space.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:56.090
What do we gain? ... We
survive and have fun.

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:58.380
If that's the kind
of thing we find fun.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.540
Right?

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:03.230
so yeah, I think by now
it should be pretty clear

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:05.470
what I'm talking about here.

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:07.630
On the other hand,
you'll probably also

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:11.140
have noticed I got more and more
into some kind of cynical tone:

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:16.520
But disgust, sarcasm, cynicism ...

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.780
... don't bring us very far.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:20.860
Why?

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:28.300
Well ... on the one hand, we won't
notice less blatant "solutions",

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.090
quote- unquote, when
it's less clear,

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.730
like, for example, when talking
about climate change.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.130
What about things
like geoengineering?

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.930
That isn't that easy?

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:42.640
And also, we're not never going
to reach those people who don't

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.860
already agree with us anyway.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:49.540
Right ... so I don't think
this is very useful.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.940
On the other hand,
I think what we

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.280
should try is to
understand what is

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:57.340
so seductive about this thing.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.220
Well, like the
world already says,

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:03.670
it solves something: good, right?

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:05.980
It solves a problem.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:08.830
Often it solves a hard
problem, a problem

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:13.640
that otherwise we wouldn't know how
to solve, how to address, even.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:17.160
It solves a problem we would
have to make sacrifices for.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.360
And we don't want that.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:22.910
Right ... and often it
just solves a problem

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:26.640
we're terribly scared about.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:31.770
So what I'm going to try
to do in this talk is

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.590
or what I think we need is
some kind of framework

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:40.080
to analyze those proposals,
a framework which does not just

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.110
ask technical questions,
because this is something

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:47.490
we are already doing
to some degree.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.180
But I think the technical
aspect is not enough.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:54.210
And so I'm going
to try to propose

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.030
a very simple
framework, a framework

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:03.010
of W questions like what, where,
when, why, who, to whom, how?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:08.410
(OK that's not a W question - anyway - ... to
help us address things in a systematic way.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:13.980
And there I'm going to focus
on the more neglected aspects.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:18.570
So I'm going to focus
on two of these aspects, let

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:22.980
me say what I mean
by the rest of them.

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:26.880
First, what does
the solution do?

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:30.050
And this should include the
complete technical workflow.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:32.260
Like, from where do
we get the data from?

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:34.630
How do we train our
machine learning models?

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:37.440
How do we evaluate them?

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.930
And in this area, we
already have some things

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:44.460
like data set documentation,
model documentation, which

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:49.760
is all great, but which is all
the technical side of things.

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:54.710
Then: where, when, and to whom
were the solution be applied?

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:58.340
This should include the
complete geographic, geographic,

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.380
sociopolitical,
et cetera context.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.680
Then: how will this
solution be applied?

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:05.690
And here really

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.990
the details matter.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:12.820
Next, who is implementing
the solution?

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:15.250
That's something I want
to talk about more.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:20.800
And also, why is the solution
being developed?

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.260
There, too, I would like to go
into some detail.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:26.920
So in other words,
in this talk, I

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:31.180
want to go into the why and
the who, because in my view,

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:35.020
these are the two aspects
which are being neglected most

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.250
in this area.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:39.400
First, let's start with the why.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.270
Why?

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:43.030
So what kind of things
you're going to hear?

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.400
Well, we care.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.670
We want to help.

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:51.310
We are here for you.

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:54.560
What kind of things won't
you hear in this area?

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.840
And here I'm kind of
splitting it up a bit.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:59.890
First, what kind of reasons
might individual people

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:02.080
have when they
implement something

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:05.860
or suggest something
which they won't say?

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:10.120
Well, for example, if
I build this thing,

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:13.270
it's going to look good on my resume.

00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:16.510
If I build this
thing, it might just

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:19.810
get me a job at company XYZ.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:26.830
If I build this thing, I might
be able to create a startup.

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:30.370
If I build this thing,
I'm going to learn

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:32.360
that crazy new technology

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:40.920
X ... and ... also it's just so cool
that this can even be done.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.680
Next, in a more indirect way...

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.080
When organizations ...

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.750
When organizations do
something, propose something,

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:53.190
what are the things
they don't say?

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:57.180
Well, if we build
this, we are going

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:00.750
to strengthen our
existing market monopoly.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:02.760
If we build this,
we're going to distract

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:06.360
from that bad thing that
recently ran through the news.

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:12.960
If we build this, we're
going to be the good guys.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:18.670
And now in a more indirect way,
let's think about side effects.

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:21.160
If we build this,
we are going to be

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:25.450
able to extract valuable data
for our targeted advertising.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:29.320
If we build this, we are
going to get data to feed back

00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:32.350
into our neural networks.

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:38.360
If we build this, we're going
to have the foot in the door.

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:43.250
If we build this ...

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:48.420
Public institutions
will be stuck with us.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:53.490
Now let's step up one level and
think ... this is about technology.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.680
And technology is
something that shapes us,

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:59.400
that forms us in our daily lives.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:04.320
If we build this, we
define how people live.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:07.950
If we build this, we
define how people think.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:12.600
If we build this, we
define what people feel.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:18.920
If we build this, we
define who people are.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:19.420
By now...

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:21.390
I think it should
be clear what I mean

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:24.100
by motivations for this thing...

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:27.840
... why things are
built. Now let's

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:32.280
switch to the next thing, the
who, who builds something.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:35.340
And here I want to be a bit
more clear from the outset who

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:39.809
I'm talking about, because this
can be a bit ambiguous, who

00:08:39.809 --> 00:08:43.570
could also mean like, to whom
the solution is being applied.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:46.690
I'm not talking about
that aspect right now.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:49.250
What I mean is ... let me spell it out.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:53.590
Who designs, implements
and hosts the solution?

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:56.140
Who processes its data?

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:59.370
Who knows how it works
and can fix problems?

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:06.290
So let's take an example.

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:08.390
And as an example,
I'm going to talk

00:09:08.390 --> 00:09:13.310
about education technology,
also abbreviated as edtech,

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:15.540
which has been booming.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:17.660
A lot over the last
years, especially,

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:21.250
of course, due to the pandemic.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:23.970
OK ... for edtech.

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:27.580
What kind of things
are you going to hear?

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.550
Well, with adaptive
technology xyz,

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:32.740
individual learners'
needs are being met.

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:35.900
With adaptive
technology xyz

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:40.960
teachers can focus on doing what
they do best. With technology

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:42.250
xyz

00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:48.070
We make learning more
effective and efficient.

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:52.040
What kind of things
won't you hear?

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.450
How it works.

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:57.150
With technology xyz we are going

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:01.290
to extract, store,
and process lots of very

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:04.370
private and personal data.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:05.940
With technology xyz

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:10.600
We are constantly
monitoring your behavior.

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.790
With technology xyz

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:13.960
YOU learn.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.615
WE'RE learning from YOU.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.430
Now this is about
education technology ...

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:26.360
what is education ... education is
like forming people, or shaping

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:29.120
young people.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:32.240
Yeah forming people,
let's just say like this.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.270
So what this really
means, like, is

00:10:35.270 --> 00:10:41.920
we define how people learn,
how we define what is learned.

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:45.490
We define what
deserves to be learned.

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:50.900
We define what deserves
to be forgotten.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:56.450
And stepping up a level,
somehow a bit more abstract.

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:57.780
What is learned?

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:01.460
Common knowledge is
building a culture.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.560
This is like, who we are.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:08.590
So what does this mean?

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:11.080
We define the past.

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.570
We define the present.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:16.440
We define the future.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.770
We define what it
means to be human.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:28.680
OK now, you may be
wondering, can you say again

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:31.560
how this is about the who?

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:35.640
Yeah, and so, before I was
saying what I mean by "who is".

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:39.480
Who designs, implements
and hosts the solution.

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:43.320
Who processes and
stores the data.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:46.360
And who knows how it works.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:48.000
This who ...

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:52.950
Or let's say, like, "these whos",
we can put them on a dimension.

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:57.540
And here I want to
ask you to go with me

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:01.890
and imagine a dimension,
a continuous dimension

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:04.740
where on the one hand,
we have the public

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:08.350
and on the other hand,
we have the private.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:11.170
On the one hand, for
the public institution,

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:14.980
I'm asking you to imagine
an ideal democracy.

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:18.040
We all know there is
no ideal democracy,

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:24.590
but we can all strive for one,
at least hope for one, perhaps.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:28.820
So on the one hand, this idea of
democracy, on the other hand,

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:31.130
for the private
institutions, this

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:33.110
can be anything, can
be a corporation,

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:35.630
a foundation, an
NGO ... doesn't really

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:38.820
matter the official status.

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:41.110
What are defining
features of this?

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.830
Who's on that dimension?

00:12:43.830 --> 00:12:47.850
For the ideal democracy
you have a democratic decision

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:52.230
process with participation
ranging on top.

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:55.870
Well, the private
end of the dimension,

00:12:55.870 --> 00:13:00.120
we can only say what's lacking,
like this democratic process

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:02.910
... otherwise could be anything.

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:07.120
What are defining values
for the public institution?

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:11.310
These are things like fairness,
justice, human rights,

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:14.120
accountability ... For the
private institution,

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:18.810
again, it will depend on
that institution's agenda.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:24.000
So now if I assume this
dimension of "whos" ...

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.660
What kind of difference
would that make?

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:28.740
For one.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:34.570
Public institutions don't have
to gather data to make money.

00:13:34.570 --> 00:13:39.700
Public institutions don't have
to keep their trade secrets.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:44.235
Public institutions don't need
to worry about market position.

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:49.930
Next, what difference
does this make

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:53.750
in political and legal respects?

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:58.940
Public institutions can be
held to ensure transparency.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:05.270
Public institutions can be held
accountable.

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:08.875
Public institutions can
be obliged to be fair.

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:17.990
And again stepping a bit
up a bit, in abstraction ...

00:14:17.990 --> 00:14:22.420
What difference does it make
to human rights and values?

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:27.190
Public institutions can be
held to prioritize values

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:29.850
over feasibility.

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:33.090
Public institutions
can be obliged

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:36.470
to respect human rights.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:39.920
Public institutions can
be held to promote, not

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:41.760
erase, individuality.

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:47.050
Now, you may be wondering...

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:49.080
Still ... I'm not a CEO...

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:51.980
What can I do?

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:54.440
Well, I don't really know.

00:14:54.440 --> 00:15:00.680
But I think one thing is,
perhaps we can make choices.

00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:02.420
This will depend.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.280
Perhaps we can make
choices like who

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:08.840
we work for, what we
vote for, whether we

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:11.370
organize politically.

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:16.230
Or one step back, perhaps even
we can question the things

00:15:16.230 --> 00:15:20.160
we are being told ... pretty much
in the spirit of this talk,

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.710
asking questions.

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:27.120
Or even perhaps
we can start

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:30.990
with a bit of imagination.

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:34.950
Maybe data science
could be different.

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.520
What if?

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:43.030
Data were used not to perpetuate,
but to change the status quo.

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:46.660
What if they were used to
make social relations more

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:50.490
egalitarian, more just?

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:55.290
What if data were used to
subvert privileges, not

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.830
reinforce them?

00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:00.850
Thank you very much
for your attention.

